<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-SEQUUS rated underperform.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-SEQUUS rated underperform.</headline>
<text>
<p>--Hanifen, Imhoff Inc said it initiated coverage of SEQUUS Pharmaceuticals Inc with an underperform rating.</p>
<p>--In a report dated January 7, Hanifen, Imhoff said its earnings per share estimates for the drug company are for a loss of $0.28 in FY97, profit of $0.20 in FY98 and profit of $0.65 in FY99.</p>
<p>--Analyst Robert Swift said he expects U.S. revenues of the company's cancer drug DOXIL will peak at less than $100 million. &quot;We believe expectations for DOXIL revenues in the short-term are too high.&quot;</p>
<p>--SEQUUS was trading at 13-3/4, off 1/4.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
